From ed07abdd93c2396c269dae43b75961a471124822 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 04:15:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] The Inner Garden, Phase 2 polish: the unboxing waits for
 the shop, Buy now once
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fixes from the phone, engineering and brand reviews of the drops:
- The unboxing is decided only once the shop has answered and the drop is
  open to members with a piece to lift, and counts as seen only when its
  pieces unfold (or on Skip). An "Opening shortly" or unreachable shop no
  longer uses it up. It now opens on the Bloom Clock's bud: the last petal
  turns out and the box rises where the bud stood.
- The pieces are laid out, unseen, before the box turns, so nothing below
  moves when they unfold (layout shift 0.43 -> 0, measured) and no render
  lands in the petal burst. The box is drawn open before its animations
  are let go, so no frame shows it shut again.
- While the shop loads or cannot be reached, the pieces are one quiet line
  (no box), never a card each.
- At the opening, a drop waiting on its pieces asks the shared catalogue
  again at once, then every 40 s, 10 times at most (ShopWatch), in the
  room, on the drops page and on the garden card.
- Buy now and Add to bag wait for each other and for the bag (bagBusy):
  a double tap opens checkout once ("Opening checkout...").
- Reduced motion and Save-Data: the "Under the petals" cover is opaque and
  the teaser is not drawn beneath it.
- The rub follows the finger after the card changes size; a second finger
  is ignored. The petal cover is calmer (4 tones, 90 petals, a gold rule).
- Press your flower: it lies down, a pressing paper comes down over it and
  lifts off the pressed specimen; the frame draws once (no blink); the
  section keeps its height. Pressed petals are askew and dried in colour.
- The Vault holds a pressed flower from the moment it is pressed; an empty
  Vault is a frame whose flower draws itself in; frames hang on gold threads.
- Bloom Clock: lining figures (no "II" for 11), petals open upward like a
  lotus fan, 4.5:1 contrast, "The next petal opens ...", and a screen
  reader is told the time only as an hour turns.
- Copy: reserve, calendar, arriving (four petals and WhatsApp), "Yours to
  see first. We share it with everyone ...", "The pieces"; the gate
  promises drops only once a drop is set.
- Manifest: optional number and names; drops.test says to delete the
  ships-empty check with the first drop. 44 px tap targets; reserve rows
  stacked; the garden tag says "Opens tomorrow · 8 pm".

Global CSS and vendor are byte-identical to origin/main; budgets measured.

